    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Embedding Provider**\n\nOkay, I've decided to use the `openai` library to generate the embeddings. I'll make the `text-embedding-ada-002` model the default. Now I need to design the process for the batch file to handle both inputs and outputs.\n\n\n**Establishing Batch Embeddings**\n\nI'm now implementing the `embed_batch.py` file. I've focused on importing the `openai` library and preparing the `generate_embeddings_batch` function. This function will take a list of texts and return embeddings generated via the `openai.embeddings.create` method. My next step involves ensuring the OpenAI provider and model are readily identifiable within the code.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867870016,
          "start": 1789867867064
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc703bb8001CW0rBaJ8fIQWJU",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc703772001YsJ78lmEBkuSf4",
      "session_id": "ses_f438fc89cffexbkLcgRNhIp44d",
      "time_created": 1789867867064,
      "time_updated": 1789867870018
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "J04N08PMiMX9M8bT",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import openai\n\ndef generate_embeddings_batch(texts: list[str], api_key: str) -> list[list[float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates embeddings for a batch of texts using OpenAI's text-embedding-ada-002 model.\n\n    Args:\n        texts: A list of strings to generate embeddings for.\n        api_key: Your OpenAI API key.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of embeddings, where each embedding is a list of floats.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = openai.OpenAI(api_key=api_key)\n    response = client.embeddings.create(\n        input=texts,\n        model=\"text-embedding-ada-002\"\n    )\n    return [item.embedding for item in response.data]\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # Replace \"YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY\" with your actual OpenAI API key\n    # It is recommended to load the API key from environment variables for production use\n    # For example: api_key = os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")\n    openai_api_key = \"YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY\" \n\n    if openai_api_key == \"YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY\":\n        print(\"Please replace 'YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY' with your actual OpenAI API key.\")\n    else:\n        sample_texts = [\n            \"This is the first sentence.\",\n            \"This is the second sentence, it is about something else.\",\n            \"And this is the third one.\",\n        ]\n        embeddings = generate_embeddings_batch(sample_texts, openai_api_key)\n        for i, embedding in enumerate(embeddings):\n            print(f\"Embedding for text {i+1}: {embedding[:5]}...\") # Print first 5 dimensions\n        print(f\"Number of embeddings generated: {len(embeddings)}\")\n        if embeddings:\n            print(f\"Dimension of each embedding: {len(embeddings[0])}\")\n",
            "filePath": "embed_batch.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
