    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Embedding Provider**\n\nOkay, I've decided to go with OpenAI's embedding API for this Python script. This seems like a solid choice given its prevalence and documentation. Now I need to figure out how to structure the code to make the provider easily swappable in the future. I'll need to define a simple interface for embedding generation.\n\n\n**Implementing OpenAI API**\n\nI've begun implementing the `embed_text.py` script. Currently, it uses the OpenAI SDK to generate text embeddings, specifically with the `text-embedding-ada-002` model. I've also incorporated a placeholder for the API key to ensure it is runnable once configured. I'm focusing on making sure the code is self-contained and ready for use.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867863750,
          "start": 1789867861349
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
